{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"ArcaniaBot","id":"810907841329627137","is_bot":1,"username":"ArcaniaBot"},"author_id":"810907841329627137","channel_id":"860203398771376198","content":"<@290612027691368454> Hello! Your long rest is over now, have a great new day in Empire City!","created_at":"2021-07-26T20:40:00.284000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"869318159117717594","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"M L","id":"290612027691368454","is_bot":0,"username":"mournfulleper"},"author_id":"290612027691368454","channel_id":"860203398771376198","content":"My memories begin six months ago. I awoke naked, a strange steam rising from my body and the smell of ozone in the air. On the floor of a ship, in the belly of the hold. In my arms I was clutching my battered and ancient brass horn. I was alone and cold, so so cold, and weak. I laid there for a time, trembling. My mind raced with all manner of strange thoughts; alchemical formulas, historical notations, scientific theorum.\nAfter a time I rose. Near to me was a large crate. \"T H E  D A V I D S O N  C O A T  C O M P A N Y\" was stenciled boldly on it's side. \"London/Pula/Shanghai/Sigil\" and underneath: \"STYLE: WINTERGREEN.\" Two of the wooden slats of the crate's lid were warped, allowing me to reach a hand through and draw out a huge green coat. As I did I saw my wrists were wet and raw with the wounds of imprisonment. I could not remember my name, or my past, only the jumbled and copius arcane encyclopedia that seemed to continue to blossom in my wracked brain.\nI shrugged into the great coat for the first time and stumbled onto the deck of a ship. A crowd of immigrants was gathered there, in awe of their first view of Empire City. I joined them. \"I hear you can be anything you want there.\" Someone near to me said. \"I hear it is a land of opportunity.\" Someone else was telling thier brother, thier children, thier cousins and friends. The voices of the hopeful washed over me, a melange of languages and tones and musical accents. I simply become one of them. Who I was before, the naked man with the horn who wore the shackles, it didn't matter who he was. I didn't want to be him anymore anyway. So when someone on the ship asked me my name, I thought about the words stitched small on the inside of my new coat. \"Call me Davidson Wintergreen\" I told them. Then I got on the first unguarded skiff I lucked into and floated away, letting the breeze carry me where it might.","created_at":"2021-07-26T23:20:06.745000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"869358451535515649","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"M L","id":"290612027691368454","is_bot":0,"username":"mournfulleper"},"author_id":"290612027691368454","channel_id":"860203398771376198","content":"It carried me into a storm. Fierce winds of war, tidal waves of fear, bombs striking like lightning.\n\nAnd now that storm has blown me away, dissipated my new identity, left me drifting and empty once again. I strain with all my might to once again recover some semblance of what was lost, to build a new man from the broken pieces left of the old. I gather everything I can of my awareness and will, focus, and begin to make myself once more.\n\n\"Who am I?\"","created_at":"2021-07-26T23:20:11.670000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"869358472192458853","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
